<!--
    Device VINTF manifest.

    The stock device has NO vendor/etc/vintf/manifest.xml. It ships
    vendor/etc/vintf/manifest_sun.xml and relies on the SKU mechanism
    (ro.boot.product.vendor.sku=sun) to pick it up. Our build invokes checkvintf
    with an empty vendor sku, so it looks for the unsuffixed manifest.xml and
    fails with "Cannot fetch vendor manifest". This file is the stock
    manifest_sun.xml content, installed at the path the build actually reads.

    Everything else is declared by the 111 per-HAL fragments under
    vendor/etc/vintf/manifest/, which the individual blob modules install
    themselves - this base manifest only carries what stock put outside a
    fragment.

    target-level 202404 is not a guess: it is what stock declares, and it is the
    truthful value because every HAL here is the stock Android 15 / SDK 35
    binary. Claiming a newer FCM level would assert compatibility the blobs do
    not have.
-->
<manifest version="8.0" type="device" target-level="202404">
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.hardware.gatekeeper</name>
        <fqname>IGatekeeper/default</fqname>
    </hal>
</manifest>
